if it's like this everywhere it would be pretty nice indeed
&quot;User agents may prompt the user when quotas are reached,&quot; &lt;- awww... spec says &quot;may&quot; :/
http://www.w3.org/TR/2009/WD-webstorage-20091029/#disk-space
cc7bcfbc58c467939c5987584fc882cb: my point is that you can't really rely on being able to store what you want to store
of course
but there should be an option to store more than 3 or 5mb if necessary
there are devices and scenarios where you are going to have less than that, I'm afraid
should be a &quot;should (if possible)&quot; then instead of a weak &quot;may&quot;
I'm really wary of user agent requirements
for user interface, that is
because, mostly users, myself included are:
a) uninterested in being interrupted by housekeeping tasks
if you don't ask (and then don't increase the alotted space)... what then? fail? truncate? both sounds sorta bad if the data is somewhat important to you... even more so if asking/increasing would have been possible
b) Not qualified to answer in such dialogs
flash for example asks... seems to work fine for them
cc7bcfbc58c467939c5987584fc882cb: I'm saying that asking the user is never fine
